  "result": "Fixed. A child `Context` now takes its own section of the parent's `default_map`, keyed by `info_name`. Before, it inherited the parent's whole map, so `{'foo': {'name': 'changed'}}` never reached the `--name` option.\n\nThe change is one line in `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py`: `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. If the parent map has no section for that command, the child gets `None`.\n\nI added `test_default_map_subcommand_section` to `tests/test_commands.py`. It checks that `foo` prints `changed` when `default_map={'foo': {'name': 'changed'}}` is passed, and `normal` when no map is passed. I did not run it against the unfixed code to confirm it fails there.\n\n`python -m pytest tests/test_commands.py tests/test_defaults.py -q` gives 145 passed. I did not run the full suite.",
